s lasered off of him by Tony Stark in  the same battle that cost copy his  shield  Bucky too might have decided to shed a  piece of his pre Civil War identity and  go forward as a non Winter Soldier Nomad  has he read his mind of all that pesky  Hydra programming at long last Sebastian  Stan has cast doubt on how well that  would work out for him telling The Daily  Beast  I think Bucky represents some of those  people that come back and just don't  know how to restart their lives  a new vision in the first new glimpse we  get a vision in infinity war he looks a  lot more human than he used to his  appearance is almost ordinary save for  the bright yellow stone embedded in his  forehead in the comics at a finding  feature of Jarvis's post download  existence is that he wants to be as  human as possible so the fact that he's  now been able to shed all the red at  least for a while means that either  someone's fantasizing about what might  have been  or he's figured out some way to  shape-shift into his desired reality in  either case he's clearly developed a  romantic relationship with the Scarlet  Witch which is also a nod to a central  component of his comics origins the two  had quite a storied relationship  throughout the years often tumultuous  but also resulting in twins named Wiccan  and Speed who both end up on the younger  vengers team during their teenage years  a certain casting call for Avengers 4  seems to indicate that the latter part  at least will come to fruition blondes  have more fun  Natasha Romanoff is another of the  exiled Avengers who seem sporting a new  look in infinity wars first glimpse  rather than the dark auburn  dude that's been her trademark all these  years she's shown with blonde locks  she's probably still a fugitive at the  start of this movie and the humor  Verdoux may just be a simple effort to  disguise herself from the government  however some suspect it might also  harken back to the comics second the  Black Widow character Yelena Bulava who  sported similarly blonde locks if she is  just trying on a new identity for size  why not make it her alter ego one  plucked from the page as a hot tip to a  comic fans frozen in time although we  don't know for sure if Thanos has or  will be able to steal the time stone  from the sanctum sanctorum there's at  least one shot in the trailer which  hints that time is being messed with in  some way as Tony Stark has shown on the  streets removing his glasses and  disbelief the rest of his friends seem  to be left in a frozen state behind him  what's more is that those mystical  shields seem to be turning very slowly  if at all does this mean that Thanos  will get his hands on that powerful  green gem despite the hero's best  efforts aura Starks somehow commanding  the time gem in the scene  time will tell Nick Fury the storyteller  although we don't actually seem in the  trailer we do get to hear Nick Fury's  voice chimed in on the group  storytelling project that tells us how  the event just  to be there was an idea he's joined by  other characters to finish out the  narrative but his inclusion is important  because the phrase is an almost exact  replica of the speech he gave in the  first Avengers movie samuel l.jackson  has said he will not appear in infinity  war Avengers 4 or black panther but  could this be a sign that something's  changed if not at least we know fury  will be there in spirit thanks for  watching click the looper icon to  subscribe to our youtube channel plus  check out all this cool stuff we know  your love to
 

